The TORS ventilation unit is designed for mounting under the upper ceiling of a room and includes standard air treatment block sets. Various configurations allow for connection with outdoor air, thereby ensuring outdoor air mixing.
• Compact size and low weight allow for easy movement and suspension of the units in the room;
• Few installation components simplify the installation of the entire unit;
• Built-in automatic control system simplifies installation work and efficiently manages equipment operation;
• The standard range allows for meticulously precise dimensions and equipment of the unit;
• Relatively low total capital costs for installing the ventilation system;
• No need for designing and installing a duct system to deliver air to the working area.

Purpose and Modes of Operation
• Ventilation and air heating systems;
• Sanitary and industrial installations;
• Smoke extraction systems.
Specifications
• General industrial (H);
• Corrosion-resistant (K1) for SEV mode only;
• Explosion-proof (V) for SEV mode in one construction scheme only;
• Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (VK1) for SEV mode in one construction scheme only.
Design
The VRAN® fans feature an impeller with backward-curved blades, available in left or right rotation, designed for high efficiency and low noise. The scroll casing is adjustable. The fans can operate in both smoke extraction (SE) and combined smoke extraction and ventilation (SEV) modes. For SEV mode, the fans are equipped with motors for continuous operation. They come with standard three-phase asynchronous single-speed motors. VRAN9 fans can be equipped with motors suitable for variable frequency speed control under the first construction scheme.
For outdoor installation (P0 and L0 casing positions) in Category 1 locations, weather protection ZONT-VRAN is available as an optional accessory.
Operation
The fans can be operated in moderate (U), moderate-cold (UHL), and tropical (T) climates, in Category 1 and 2 locations according to GOST 15150.
Operating Conditions
• Ambient temperature:
• from -45 to +40°C for moderate climate;
• from -60 to +40°C for moderate and cold climate;

VIR150 fans are designed for moving air and dust-laden gas mixtures with dust concentrations up to 20 g/m³ in dry air and up to 5 g/m³ in humid (saturated) air.
Due to their design features and aerodynamic parameters, VIR150 series fans can be used for local exhaust systems with complex multi-stage filtration systems, as well as for other technological needs requiring high pressure at very low air flow rates.
Operating Modes:
• T80 - medium temperature up to 80°C;
• T150 - medium temperature up to 150°C (only for scheme 1);
• T200 - medium temperature up to 200°C (only for schemes 3 and 5);
• T300 - medium temperature up to 300°C (only for schemes 3 and 5).
Specifications:
- General industrial (N);
- Corrosion-resistant (K1);
- Explosion-proof (V) – only for T80 and schemes 1 and 5;
- Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (VK1) – only for T80 and schemes 1 and 5;
- Spark-proof (I).
VIR150 fans have an impeller of RD and LG rotation directions with backward-curved blades of special shape, ensuring high efficiency and low noise.
The fully welded spiral casing is adjustable.
VIR150 fans are manufactured in two modifications:
Normal (nominal) impeller size Dk = Dn;
Reduced impeller size Dk = 0.95 Dn (except for scheme 5).
Fans of modification 2 are produced in sizes 063…090.
Fans are equipped with standard three-phase asynchronous electric motors 380 V~50 Hz.

Purpose and Operating Mode:
⦁ Ventilation systems – operating mode: T80;
⦁ Sanitary and industrial installations – operating modes: T80, T200.
Configurations:
⦁ General industrial (H);
⦁ Corrosion-resistant (K1);
⦁ Explosion-proof (V);
⦁ Explosion-proof (VS) – for gas group IIC, hydrogen only, according to GOST R 55026-2012;
⦁ Explosion-proof and corrosion-resistant (VK1);
⦁ Explosion-proof and corrosion-resistant (VSK1) – for gas group IIC, hydrogen only, according to GOST R 55026-2012.
Features:
KROV® fans have a low-profile housing with free air discharge upwards and a lightweight design; they feature special protection against atmospheric precipitation.
The impeller, with an increased efficiency (up to 75%), is directly mounted on the motor shaft and consumes power that does not overload the motor as the airflow increases.
Fans generate high airflow, high static pressure, and low noise.
Fans are equipped with high-quality three-phase asynchronous single-speed motors. Frequency control of the rotation speed is possible.
Mounting dimensions on the base plate are standardized with KROS® roof fans.
Roof fans are easily installed using the STAM® mounting cup.
Additional fan configurations and options are available – see the "Additional Equipment" section of the catalog.

Purpose and operating mode:
1. Ventilation and air heating systems;
2. Smoke control systems (PD);
3. Sanitary and technological installations.
Configuration:
⦁ General Industrial (H);
⦁ Corrosion-resistant (K);
⦁ Explosion-proof (V);
⦁ Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (VK).
OSA® 300 series low and medium pressure axial fans consist of a newly designed impeller, a fully welded rolled housing of an asynchronous motor located within the casing.
The motor support strut is aerodynamically shaped and acts as a straightening device.
The impeller is equipped with adjustable blades that are turned backward to achieve maximum efficiency. The blades are volumetric, cast under pressure. The live cross-sectional area of the airflow is maximized, significantly reducing the exit velocity. Thanks to the new impeller design, the fans are designed with the highest static efficiency at static pressure values of 100 - 900 Pa.
The fan casing flanges are flanged, providing increased rigidity and precision, ensuring a uniform minimum radial gap between the impeller blades and the casing perimeter.
The casing is made of aluminum, stainless steel, or carbon steel.
In the absence of a network at the inlet, an inlet collector VKO-OSA or a toroidal adapter PET-OSA should be used.
The flow direction is always from the impeller to the motor, regardless of orientation.

Configuration:
⦁ General Industrial (H);
⦁ Corrosion-resistant (K);
⦁ Explosion-proof (B)(1);
⦁ Explosion-proof (BS)(1) for gas group IIC (hydrogen);
⦁ Explosion-proof (BP)(1) for group IIIC (conductive dust);
⦁ Explosion-proof Corrosion-resistant (BK)(1);
⦁ Explosion-proof Corrosion-resistant (BSK)(1) for gas group IIC (hydrogen);
⦁ Explosion-proof Corrosion-resistant (BPK)(1) for group IIIC (conductive dust).
(1) only for fans with aluminum blades.
Purpose:
⦁ Ventilation and air heating systems.
⦁ Smoke control (PD) and support ventilation systems.
⦁ Sanitary and technological installations.
OSA®-EVO low and medium pressure axial fans consist of a fully welded rolled housing, a uniquely patented VEZA impeller design, and an asynchronous motor or a permanent magnet motor housed within the casing. The role of the support strut is performed by a straightening apparatus (SA) with fixed aluminum blades. The impeller is a dismantlable hub with adjustable blades, consisting of a main hub for blade installation, a clamping hub for fixing the blades, and a hub shroud. The blades are volumetric and cast under pressure.
The fan casing flanges are flanged, providing increased rigidity and precision, ensuring a uniform minimum radial gap between the blades and the casing perimeter.
The casing is made of carbon steel with subsequent powder coating or stainless steel.

Configuration:
• General Industrial (H);
• Corrosion-resistant (•K1 •K3);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Explosion-proof (VS) - for gas group IIC;
• Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (•VK1 •VK3);
• Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (•VSK1 •VSK3) - for gas group IIC.
Purpose:
• Ventilation and air heating systems - operating mode: •T80;
• Sanitary and production installations - operating mode: •T80 •T200.
VRAV® fans have a drum-type impeller with specially shaped forward-curved blades for left or right rotation.
The spiral casing is adjustable.
The fans are equipped with standard three-phase asynchronous single-speed motors.
For the housing position PO (LO) for placement category 1 (outdoor), protection against atmospheric precipitation ZONT-VRAV (ordered separately as an option) is provided; for the housing position P90 (LO), a canopy (KOZYREK) is available (ordered separately as an option).
Additional equipment options for the fans are available, see the "Additional Equipment" section in the catalog.
The fans can be operated in conditions of moderate (U), moderate and cold (UHL), and tropical climates of placement categories 1 and 2 according to GOST 15150.
Operating conditions:
• Ambient temperature:
o from -45 to +40°C for moderate climate, o from -60 to +40°C for moderate and cold climate, o from -10 to +50°C for tropical climate;

Configuration:
• General Industrial (H);
• Corrosion-resistant (•K1 •K3);
• Explosion-proof (V) - only for 1 design scheme execution;
• Explosion-proof (VS) - for gas group IIC hydrogen only according to GOST R 55026-2012; only for 1 design scheme execution;
• Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (•VK1 •VK3) - only for 1 design scheme execution;
• Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (•VSK1 •VSK3) - for gas group IIC hydrogen only according to GOST R 55026-2012; only for 1 design scheme execution.
Purpose:
• Ventilation and air heating systems - operating mode: •T80;
• Sanitary and production installations - operating mode: •T80 •T200.
VRAN® fans have a drum-type impeller with specially shaped backward-curved blades for left or right rotation, ensuring high efficiency and low noise.
The spiral casing is adjustable.
The fans are equipped with standard three-phase asynchronous single-speed motors. For VRAN9 fans in the 1 design scheme, motors allowing frequency control of rotation speed are available.
For housing position PO (LO) for placement category 1 (outdoor), protection against atmospheric precipitation ZONT-VRAN (ordered separately as an option) is provided; for housing position P90 (LO), a canopy (KOZYREK) is available (ordered separately as an option).
Additional equipment options for the fans are available, see the "Additional Equipment" section in the catalog.

The control unit "Vector" (UR "Vector") is designed to automatically control the parameters of the heat (cold) carrier and ensure its circulation when connecting supply ventilation systems (heat exchangers, air heaters, air coolers), or other systems (air heating – heating units, heat curtains) thermal energy consumption to heat(cold)the source.
SD "Vector" is a set of piping, shut-off, regulating, protective (if available in the scheme) fittings, pumping equipment (if available in the scheme), instrumentation and control systems (if available in the scheme).
The design of the UR "Vector" is determined by the schemes:
 1 — smooth regulation;
 2 — mixing with smooth control;
 3 — deflecting contour;
 4 — deflecting contour with mixing;
 5 — mixing circuit without reinforcement in the mixing branch;
 5M — modification of scheme 5 (added fittings in the mixing branch);
 6 — open/closed;
 6M — open/closed with pump.
Modification of circuits:
P is a modification of the circuits equipped with a backup pump.
The modification with a backup (P) pump is used when there is a need for 100% backup of the pump. There is 1 pump operating normally, and it switches to a backup pump if necessary.
A modification with a backup pump is available for the following schemes: 2P, 4P, 5P, 5MP.
And – A modification of the intellect equipped with an energy-efficient pump.

NERPA®-KO are high-density non-return air dampers (leakage class 2) with increased structural rigidity of the housing and blades, designed for automatically shutting off air ducts when the fan is turned off. NERPA®-KO non-return dampers operate on a gravity-based principle and are designed to work in high-pressure ventilation networks under conditions of sharp pressure drops in the network, as well as for sealing the internal volume of ventilation networks.
Versions:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (KV).
Construction
NERPA®-KO dampers consist of a reinforced welded housing and box-shaped blades. The blade junction is designed as a lock seal. Sealing is achieved with a special silicone profile mounted on the blade or housing stops. The damper’s kinematics include levers and rigidly coupled rods. The dampers are made in duct execution and have two connection flanges.
NERPA®-KO dampers are made of carbon thick-sheet steel with protective coating (versions • N • V) or stainless steel (versions • K • KV).
The dampers are certified according to the TR TS 012/2011 regulation. In explosion-proof dampers, certified EPV electric drives of VEZA's own production in steel with protective coating or stainless steel housings are used.

Fire overpressure dampers OXID are designed to compensate for the volumes of removed combustion products in rooms protected by exhaust smoke ventilation by compensatory supply of outside air from airlock vestibules or elevator shafts according to paragraph 8.8 of the code SP 7.13.130.2013.
The dampers are intended for installation in the barriers of airlock vestibules or elevator shafts directly adjacent to the protected rooms.
Versions:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Frost-resistant (MS);
• Frost-resistant corrosion-resistant (MSK).
Type of damper:
• Wall (1*φ);
• Duct (2*φ).
The dampers are made of a rectangular housing of galvanized (versions N, MS) or stainless (versions K, MSK) steel, with one or more rotating type blades installed inside. The blade is made of fire-resistant material characterized by low thermal conductivity, moisture resistance, frost resistance, and environmental friendliness. Inside the housing, there is a spring mechanism for adjusting the pressure at which the damper starts to open, adjusted during the commissioning of the smoke ventilation system.
In frost-resistant versions (MS/MSK), the dampers are equipped with a flexible self-regulating heating cable (heating element) to prevent blade freezing.
The design of the damper prevents the blade from protruding beyond the dimensions of the housing.

Universal fire dampers KPU-1N are designed for automatic closure of ventilation ducts or openings in building structures and are installed in general ventilation, air conditioning, exhaust and supply smoke ventilation systems, as well as systems for removing gas and smoke after a fire from premises protected by gas, aerosol, or powder fire extinguishing systems.
IMPORTANT! KPU-1N rectangular duct-type dampers remain operational regardless of spatial orientation, but with the condition of horizontal blade axis positioning. Wall-type KPU dampers remain operational only with vertical installation and vertical blade axis positioning.
Purpose:
• Normally open (O);
• Normally closed (Z).
The dampers consist of a rectangular section body made of galvanized (executions •N •MS •V •VMS) or stainless steel (executions •K •MSK •VK •VMSK) with an internally installed rotating blade. The blade is entirely made of fire-resistant material without metal cladding, characterized by low thermal conductivity, moisture resistance, frost resistance, and environmental friendliness.
Versions without blade protrusion (for duct type) are available.
Design:
The actuator in the duct-type damper is located only outside the damper, in the wall-type damper - inside the damper.
Execution:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Frost-resistant (MS);
• Frost-resistant corrosion-resistant (MSK);

Universal fire dampers KPU-2H are designed for automatic blocking of ventilation channels or openings in building structures and are installed in general ventilation, air conditioning, exhaust and supply smoke ventilation systems, as well as systems for removing gas and smoke after a fire from rooms protected by gas, aerosol, or powder fire extinguishing installations.
IMPORTANT! KPU-2H channel type dampers of rectangular cross-section maintain functionality regardless of spatial orientation, but with the condition of horizontal placement of their blade rotation axis. KPU® wall-type dampers maintain functionality only when installed vertically and with the vertical placement of the blade rotation axis.
Purpose:
• Normally open (O);
• Normally closed (Z);
• Smoke (D).
Execution:
• Explosion-proof frost-resistant corrosion-resistant (VMSK);
• General industrial (H);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Frost-resistant (MS);
• Frost-resistant corrosion-resistant (MSK);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Explosion-proof corrosion-resistant (VK);
• Explosion-proof frost-resistant (VMS).

KPU-3 universal fire dampers are designed to automatically close ventilation ducts or openings in building enclosing structures and are installed in general ventilation, air conditioning, smoke exhaust and smoke supply systems, as well as in systems removing gas and smoke after a fire from rooms protected by gas, aerosol or powder fire-extinguishing installations.
IMPORTANT: duct-type KPU-3 dampers of rectangular section remain operable in any spatial orientation, provided the blade rotation axis is horizontal.
Purpose:
• Normally open (O);
• Normally closed (Z);
• Smoke (D).
Design:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Frost-resistant (MS);
• Frost-resistant corrosion-resistant (MSK).

KEDR® and KEDR®-S are high-density valves designed for regulating intake, recirculation, or exhaust air in high-pressure ventilation systems, as well as for sealing the internal volume of ventilation networks, with operating pressure up to 2500 Pa. Additionally, one of the targeted purposes of these valves is their use as shut-off valves in medium-pressure systems where multiple fans operate asynchronously.
In this case, the valves are installed directly on the exhaust and/or intake side of the fan and are used to prevent the reverse spinning of the wheel of a non-operational fan, which is unacceptable if the fan can start automatically.
The KEDR®-S valve is a frost-resistant version of the KEDR® valve, ensuring reliable operation under extreme humidity and low temperatures down to minus 60°C.
Execution:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (KV).
The KEDR® and KEDR®-S valve consists of a reinforced box-shaped body made of steel. The blades are made of special volumetric steel profile and do not extend beyond the body. The valve kinematics include levers and rods on a rigid coupling. Bearing units prevent misalignment of the blade axes under pressure, allowing seamless flow regulation under maximum pressure conditions.

NERPA®-KO is a high-density air check valve (leakage class 2), with increased rigidity of the body and blade structure, designed to automatically close ducts when the fan is off. NERPA®-KO check valves have a gravity action type and are intended for use in high-pressure ventilation networks under conditions of sharp pressure changes in the network, as well as for sealing the internal volume of ventilation networks.
Design:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (KV).
NERPA®-KO check valves consist of: rectangular - reinforced welded box body, round - solid round body (i.e., the valve flange is made "integrally" with the main body material and has no welded joint, which significantly increases the rigidity and geometry of the body), the blade is made hollow box-shaped. A special silicone sealing profile is fixed around the perimeter of the internal cross-section of the body.
Bearing units ensure low friction losses, allowing the valve to open easily across the entire declared range of airflow speeds. The valve is made in channel design and has two connecting flanges.
NERPA®-KO valves are made of carbon thick-sheet steel with a protective coating (version • N) or stainless steel (version • K • KV).

TYULPAN® is a gravity check valve of the petal type. It differs from conventional (single-blade) check valves in its low actuation inertia and lower regulated minimum airflow speed required for its opening. The blades of such valves open under the influence of the airflow and automatically return to their original closed position when the air supply stops. This valve is especially relevant for use with axial fans, which generally have lower outlet airflow speeds compared to radial fans.
Design:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (KV).
The TYULPAN® valve is presented in three main models:
• TYULPAN®-1 - for operation on horizontal duct sections (installed vertically);
• TYULPAN®-2 - for operation on vertical duct sections (installed horizontally) when the airflow moves from bottom to top (for exhaust);
• TYULPAN®-3 - for operation on vertical duct sections (installed horizontally) when the airflow moves from top to bottom (for supply).
The TYULPAN® valve consists of a box body and profiled blades installed in the body on axes and made of steel. The blades of the TYULPAN® valve are joined by a lock. There is no blade overhang beyond the body dimensions.
Manufacturing material - galvanized (version • N • V) or stainless (version • K • KV) steel.

UKOL is a check valve designed to automatically close the duct section to prevent free air transfer in ventilation systems when the fan is off, and to reduce heat losses. The blades of such a valve are filled with insulating material, and the body is made with a thermal break.
Design:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K).
UKOL valves are presented in three main types:
● UKOL-1 – for operation on horizontal duct sections (installed vertically);
● UKOL-2 – for operation on vertical duct sections (installed horizontally) when the airflow moves from bottom to top (for exhaust);
● UKOL-3 – for operation on vertical duct sections (installed horizontally) when the airflow moves from top to bottom (for supply).
The valves are made in rectangular or round sections and consist of two half-bodies, between which an insulating material spacer is installed. In the spacer area, there is one or more box-shaped blades, inside which insulation is placed.
Manufacturing material - galvanized (version ● N) or stainless (version ● K) steel.

REGULAR® is a universal air valve designed for use in ventilation and air conditioning systems.
Design:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (KV).
The REGULAR® valve consists of a body and blades made of profiled sheet metal. The manufacturing material is galvanized (design "N" and "V") or stainless (design "K" and "KV") steel. The valve has a special spring seal on the blade ends. The blade mating is made in the form of a lock seal with a seal located in the mating area. For transmitting torque from the actuator, a system of steel levers and rods is used.
Electric actuators are selected depending on the valve's working cross-sectional area in accordance with the equipment table. REGULAR® valves have a modern appearance that meets the current consumer requirements for the design of most types of premises.
Since the valve blade is made of steel profile obtained on the profiling line, to optimize the live cross-section of this valve, it is necessary to select the height H = 100/150/170/250/300/320/470/620/770/920/1070/1220/1370/1520/1670/ 1820/1970/2120/2270/ 2420 mm. Valves with heights different from these will be manufactured with a cross-section close to standardized sizes H but with a higher stopper (with less "live" cross-section).

REGULAR®-L is a universal air valve created based on the REGULAR® valve and designed to regulate the flow of supply, recirculation, or exhaust air in ventilation and air conditioning systems in smooth regulation and "open/close" modes without leakage requirements in the closed state. The REGULAR®-L valve can also be used as a throttling device.
Design:
• General industrial (N);
• Corrosion-resistant (K);
• Explosion-proof (V);
• Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (KV).
REGULAR®-L valves consist of a solid-drawn round body and a sheet metal blade. The manufacturing material is galvanized (design • N • V) or stainless (design • K • KV) steel. REGULAR®-L valves do not have any seals in their composition.
Standardly, the valves can be equipped with HEMAH electric actuators. Custom manufacturing of valves with BELIMO electric actuators or electric actuators from other manufacturers is available upon request.
The valves are certified according to the regulation TR CU 012/2011. Explosion-proof valves use certified EPV electric actuators of our own production by VEZA LLC in steel with a protective coating or stainless steel bodies. Custom manufacturing of valves with explosion-proof electric actuators from other manufacturers is available upon request.

UPVK devices are designed to prevent the impact of an air shock wave (ASW) and to isolate buildings from the external environment when an ASW occurs; they are installed at outdoor air intake and exhaust air discharge points. UPVK ensures safety and keeps its mechanical strength and operability under ASW impact. UPVK devices are made in three basic designs by flow direction and blast wave impact:
1 – ASW and working medium move in the same direction;
2 – ASW and working medium move in opposite directions;
3 – double-acting.
Design:
- General industrial (N);
- Explosion-proof (V);
- Corrosion-resistant explosion-proof (K).
UPVK consists of a welded four-wall box-shaped casing and rotary blades turning in bearing units. It is made in duct design with two connecting flanges. The blades are returned to the working position manually with a wrench. A protective mesh prevents foreign objects that could block the blades from entering the device. In the normal (standby) position the UPVK blades are always open due to spring action.

The casing of the fan made of galvanized steel provides reliable protection against corrosion. All sizes of Kanal-PKV are equipped with a service cover. The service cover is necessary for direct access to the impeller and motor during installation or maintenance of the fan.
The sound-insulated casing distinguishes the Kanal-PKV-Sh from the standard series. The casing is made of galvanized steel and has a box-like structure. The space between the walls of the sound-insulated casing is filled with non-combustible wool, characterized by high sound insulation properties.
The impellers of Kanal-PKV-Sh duct fans with forward-curved blades are made of galvanized steel and undergo thorough static and dynamic balancing.
Asynchronous single- or three-phase motors with an external rotor are characterized by low power consumption and significant operational life. The standard equipment of duct fan motors includes a thermal contact relay, ensuring comprehensive thermal protection.
Fans of this type can be installed in any spatial position, provided there is free access to the fan's service cover.
●Used in rooms with increased noise level requirements and produced in a sound-insulated casing;
●Ensure ease of installation and maintenance in confined spaces;
● Universally compatible with other elements of duct ventilation systems;

The valves have a round casing with a blade installed inside. This design ensures a proportional dependence of the air flow through the valve on the blade's angle of rotation.
Structural elements of the valve are made of galvanized steel.
The valve can be made:
•
shut-off type – the valve casing lacks an air flow selection nomogram. The valve blade additionally has a rubber seal to reduce leaks in the closed position;
•
regulating type – the valve casing has an air flow nomogram depending on the pressure drop and the blade's angle of rotation. The valve blade is without a rubber seal.
As actuators, the following can be used:
• manual drive for local manual control;
• electric drive for remote valve control;
• the valve maintains operability regardless of spatial orientation;
• designed for regulating the flow of supply and exhaust air in duct ventilation and air conditioning systems;
• can be used for air recirculation;
• used for sealing the internal volume of ventilation networks;
• the processed air must be conditioned, should not contain solid, fibrous, sticky, or aggressive impurities;
• allowable dust and solid impurities content not exceeding 0.1 g/m³.

The smoke vent DYMOSOR®-500 is designed for installation on building roofs with a slope angle of more than 14 degrees and for use in natural draft smoke ventilation systems. Besides its primary function of removing combustion products, it can be used for room ventilation. In the version with a transparent cover, it also provides additional natural lighting for the room.
Versions:
• Standard (S);
• Modular (M);
• Modular-left (ML);
• Modular-right (MR).
Body:
• Straight, 100 mm high, made of cold-rolled sheet metal;
• Support flange at the bottom for attachment to the roof structure;
• 50 mm thick mineral wool thermal insulation;
• Heating cable installed to prevent the cover from freezing in cold weather;
• For M/ML/MR versions, structural elements are provided for connecting 500 series hatches.
•
Cover:
• One rotating in three types;
• Attached to the body with multi-axis hinges. The cover opening angle is at least 90 degrees;
• Equipped with a limit switch;
• The type of cover should be chosen considering the required heat transfer resistance, regulated by SP 50.13330.2012 for the specific climatic region.
Actuating mechanism:
• One rod electric drive, branded by VEZA, powered at 24V, with a force of 1600/3000N, placed inside the hatch under the cover.

The aeration hatch AEROZOR®-100 is designed for installation on flat roofs or with a slope angle of up to 14 degrees and for covering openings in the exterior horizontal enclosing structures of the building. It is also used in natural ventilation mode (airing) of the room. In the version with a transparent cover, it also provides additional natural lighting for the room.
Versions:
• Standard (S);
• Modular (M);
• Modular-left (ML);
• Modular-right (MR).
Body:
• Straight, 500 mm high with a 10-degree slope, made of galvanized steel;
• Support flange at the bottom for attachment to the roof structure;
• 50 mm thick foil-coated mineral wool thermal insulation;
• Wind protection screens – deflectors are installed in the hatches to increase ventilation efficiency by changing aerodynamics;
• For M/ML/MR versions, structural elements are provided for connecting hatches/lights.
Cover:
• Single flap rotating in three types;
• Consists of a steel load-bearing frame made of cold-rolled sheet metal and filling. Attached to the base with multi-axis hinges, cover opening angle of at least 90 degrees. Hinges located inside the product, eliminating icing, facilitating more convenient and quality installation of waterproof roofing material;
• The type of cover should be chosen considering the required heat transfer resistance, regulated by SP 50.13330.2012 for the specific climatic region.

The KHODOZOR®-100 roof hatch is designed for installation on a flat roof or with a roof pitch angle up to 14 degrees, covering openings in the building's external horizontal enclosing structures, and providing personnel access to the roof for repairs and other maintenance work.
Body:
• Straight, 500 mm high with a 10-degree pitch, made of galvanized steel;
• Features a support flange at the bottom for attachment to the roof structure;
• Thermal insulation made of 50 mm thick foil-faced mineral wool;
• The hatch body has latches with holes for a padlock to prevent unauthorized access to the roof.
Cover:
• Single-bladed, available in three types;
• Consists of a steel load-bearing frame made of cold-rolled sheet metal and filling. Attached to the base with multi-axis hinges, the cover opens at an angle of at least 90 degrees. Hinges are located inside the product, preventing freezing and facilitating convenient and quality installation of roofing waterproofing material;
• Cover type selection should consider the required heat transfer resistance, regulated by SP 50.13330.2012 for the specific climate region.
Actuator:
• KHODOZOR® hatches are not equipped with an electric drive but have two gas springs located on the inner sides of the hatch.
Painting:
• Powder coating in signal gray RAL 7012;
• Custom colors available upon request according to the RAL catalog.

The NEBOZOR®-200 blank skylight is designed for installation on a flat roof or with a roof pitch angle up to 14 degrees, covering openings in the building's external horizontal enclosing structures, and providing natural lighting to rooms under the flat roof in normal operating conditions where additional ventilation or roof access is not required.
Versions:
• Standard (S);
• Modular (M);
• Modular-end (MT).
Body:
• Straight, 500 mm high with a 10-degree pitch, made of galvanized steel;
• Features a support flange at the bottom for attachment to the roof structure;
