Central frame-panel marine air conditioners KOMPAS-BOV are designed to create and maintain artificial climate parameters in the serviced premises of sea-going vessels of mixed and inland navigation of all classes, types, and purposes by treating and supplying air. These air conditioners enable a complete range of air treatment processes: cleaning, dehumidifying, humidifying, cooling, heating, etc.
KOMPAS-BOV air conditioners are intended for use on gas extraction platforms, floating drilling rigs, stationary marine platforms, civil and industrial construction facilities. The distinguishing feature of this type of air conditioner is its compactness, seismic resistance, vibration resistance, trim and heel resistance, natural aggressive environments (marine air, high daily temperature differences), comparative ease of installation, and competitive price.
KOMPAS-BOV air conditioners have a modular system of equipment layout, allowing the assembly of installations of any complexity from blocks and parts of sections produced at the enterprise. Modular sections are mounted to each other on elastic vibration-proof gaskets. This air conditioner consists of the following units:
• Frame-panel casing;
• Air heater;
• Air cooler;
• Air filters;
• Fan and motor;
• Mixing chamber;
• Additional sections (on request) - electric heater, humidifier, recuperator, etc.
